WEBVTT

00:48.673 --> 00:50.216
EMERGENCY

01:04.272 --> 01:06.024
This is Chief Team Two.

01:06.858 --> 01:08.109
Yes.

01:09.569 --> 01:11.029
What? An accident?

01:16.493 --> 01:18.745
An accident? What accident?

01:20.205 --> 01:21.539
Did someone get hurt?

01:29.380 --> 01:30.673
Hurry up.

01:34.511 --> 01:35.637
Hurry up.

01:36.513 --> 01:38.264
Doctor!

01:38.348 --> 01:39.599
It's an emergency patient.

01:41.309 --> 01:42.727
Male in his late 20s.

01:42.811 --> 01:46.147
He was injured in an explosion,
and he can't open his eyes.

01:46.231 --> 01:47.565
His vitals are 100 over 60, 120bpm.

01:47.649 --> 01:49.818
- This way. Hurry.
- Okay.

01:51.903 --> 01:54.114
- Does he have a guardian?
- Here.

01:54.197 --> 01:55.323
I'm his guardian.

01:55.824 --> 01:57.534
Can you tell me his name first?

01:58.326 --> 02:00.912
Lee Si-woo. He works at the KMA.

02:02.872 --> 02:04.249
Oh, no.

02:05.083 --> 02:06.459
Why? Who is it?

02:07.502 --> 02:08.670
It's Forecaster Lee.

02:14.509 --> 02:16.302
He's badly hurt and in the hospital.

02:25.145 --> 02:26.938
You should go, Forecaster Lee.

02:31.526 --> 02:32.569
Go where?

02:32.652 --> 02:34.320
To the Jeju Typhoon Center.

02:34.404 --> 02:35.446
You should go.

02:39.868 --> 02:41.035
Do you mean that?

02:41.744 --> 02:44.205
I'm never half-hearted
when it comes to work.

02:46.207 --> 02:47.208
That means

02:47.876 --> 02:50.253
you've already made up your mind.

02:51.880 --> 02:54.591
Yes. If it's all right with you.

02:57.552 --> 02:59.846
When body temperature drops by 1°C,

03:00.471 --> 03:04.100
our body's immune system
weakens by as much as 30 percent.

03:05.435 --> 03:08.771
Ha-kyung doesn't sincerely date anyone
if they're not a marriage prospect.

03:10.189 --> 03:11.232
You knew that, right?

03:12.317 --> 03:13.902
This means that

03:14.485 --> 03:16.571
you become vulnerable to external attacks.

03:19.991 --> 03:21.117
What?

03:21.951 --> 03:23.244
What are you talking about?

03:23.328 --> 03:24.746
I want some time apart.

03:25.747 --> 03:27.749
I think that's best for both of us.

03:28.791 --> 03:29.918
Yu-jin.

03:30.001 --> 03:32.003
We need some time to think.

03:32.086 --> 03:34.047
Let's evaluate our relationship.

03:36.007 --> 03:38.343
Be honest. You need some time alone too.

03:45.975 --> 03:50.188
There's still time,
so think about it and let me know.

03:52.607 --> 03:53.733
No.

03:54.984 --> 03:55.985
I'll go.

03:56.653 --> 03:58.071
You can think about it.

03:58.154 --> 04:01.574
I don't have to. It's work.

04:02.867 --> 04:03.952
I'll go.

04:09.457 --> 04:10.667
Okay.

04:14.796 --> 04:16.839
Do you have anything else to say?

04:16.923 --> 04:18.258
No.

04:22.845 --> 04:24.097
All right.

04:32.814 --> 04:35.483
The same goes for
the temperature between people.

04:40.822 --> 04:42.573
If you leave like this,

04:42.657 --> 04:44.117
it's really over between us.

04:45.702 --> 04:47.620
Have you thought about that?

04:52.208 --> 04:53.626
If that's what you want,

04:54.669 --> 04:55.503
we can do that.

05:15.815 --> 05:19.485
The 77-4 bus will be arriving shortly.

05:48.973 --> 05:50.767
There are times

05:51.350 --> 05:53.478
when even the smallest word

05:54.103 --> 05:57.648
or even the smallest expression can turn
the temperature of our heart cold.

05:59.817 --> 06:00.985
And…

06:07.283 --> 06:09.702
There was an accident?
How badly hurt is he?

06:10.328 --> 06:12.914
No, who am I speaking to?

06:12.997 --> 06:15.541
- Can you tell me what hospital--
- This is Chae Yu-jin.

06:25.134 --> 06:27.261
I'm with Si-woo right now.

06:28.262 --> 06:32.475
As soon as the temperature
of our heart drops even by one degree,

06:33.101 --> 06:36.646
we can't help
but become sensitive and vulnerable

06:37.438 --> 06:39.273
to all external environments.

06:53.121 --> 06:58.126
EPISODE 11
1

06:58.209 --> 07:00.169
2 DAYS AGO

07:49.427 --> 07:51.304
The continuous heatwave

07:51.387 --> 07:54.182
is exhausting
our body and mind these days.

07:54.265 --> 07:57.310
A heatwave advisory has been issued
in most parts of the west

07:57.393 --> 07:59.228
and the Yeongnam area today,

07:59.312 --> 08:02.440
and a heatwave warning
is also in effect in Gwangju.

08:05.776 --> 08:07.153
INNOVATIVE WEATHER SERVICES
A STEPPING STONE TO PUBLIC SAFETY

08:07.904 --> 08:10.531
Jeez. No news of rain?

08:10.615 --> 08:11.866
Less than 5mm of rain will fall

08:11.949 --> 08:14.535
on the east coast
due to the influence of the east wind,

08:14.619 --> 08:16.662
but it'll be limited
to some areas of Gangwon.

08:17.246 --> 08:19.499
We can't call it rain then.

08:20.333 --> 08:22.293
Goodness, it's burning red.

08:22.376 --> 08:24.962
The Ministry of the Interior and Safety
will announce on the news

08:25.046 --> 08:26.631
what to do in the event of a heatwave.

08:26.714 --> 08:30.301
And local governments will put more effort
into securing heat reduction facilities.

08:30.384 --> 08:31.344
Okay.

08:31.427 --> 08:35.014
The local government offices
will be worn out.

08:35.097 --> 08:37.266
- What can we do?
- What do you want to do this weekend?

08:37.350 --> 08:39.727
It's the last weekend before I leave.

08:40.561 --> 08:41.979
What are you doing?

08:42.563 --> 08:43.773
What?

08:45.816 --> 08:46.859
Aren't we in a meeting?

08:47.568 --> 08:48.569
Yes.

08:48.653 --> 08:51.197
Please prepare an impact forecast
for each region.

08:52.657 --> 08:54.659
How about duck soup in Gapyeong?

08:55.243 --> 08:57.119
Especially duck soup in Gapyeong…

08:57.203 --> 08:58.162
What?

09:05.503 --> 09:06.546
I'm sorry.

09:07.046 --> 09:09.549
Especially in the southern
and western coastal areas,

09:09.632 --> 09:12.677
please control the water temperature
and install shading nets in farms.

09:13.761 --> 09:15.471
Please ask the media to refrain

09:15.555 --> 09:17.765
from making provocative comments
regarding the heatwave.

09:17.848 --> 09:19.225
I'll do my best.

09:19.308 --> 09:20.309
Okay.

09:20.810 --> 09:23.062
That's all for today's meeting.

09:23.145 --> 09:24.981
- Well done.
- Good work.

09:25.064 --> 09:26.357
- Good work.
- Good work.

09:26.440 --> 09:28.568
Duck soup in Gapyeong sounds good.

09:29.151 --> 09:31.529
By the way, have you decided?

09:33.573 --> 09:36.117
- Who's going to the typhoon center?
- Oh, yes.

09:36.659 --> 09:39.537
- Is it already that time of the year?
- Yes, it is.

09:39.620 --> 09:41.205
Who's going this time?

09:41.289 --> 09:43.291
I don't know, but I hope it isn't me.

09:46.961 --> 09:48.421
Haven't you decided yet?

09:51.257 --> 09:52.592
I'm going.

09:54.135 --> 09:56.887
What? When was it decided?

09:56.971 --> 09:58.139
Yesterday.

09:59.056 --> 10:01.434
- Congratulations on being chosen.
- Congratulations.

10:02.476 --> 10:04.812
Forecaster Lee and Director Jin,
come to my office.

10:04.895 --> 10:06.063
Yes, sir.

10:10.985 --> 10:13.446
Hi, Bo-mi. Yes.

10:15.156 --> 10:16.657
Okay.

10:17.199 --> 10:19.243
I want to go to Jeju Island.

10:19.785 --> 10:21.829
You seem excited to go to Jeju Island.

10:21.912 --> 10:24.665
No, I'm excited
to go to the typhoon center.

10:24.749 --> 10:26.792
I've always wanted to work there.

10:26.876 --> 10:29.086
You know I like to be on site.

10:29.170 --> 10:31.380
You said you wanted
to work at Headquarters.

10:31.464 --> 10:33.132
Now you want to be on site.

10:33.215 --> 10:35.676
Because I'm quite good
at handling multiple tasks.

10:36.802 --> 10:39.388
That's great. Good luck to you.

10:39.472 --> 10:42.391
Why are you acting like this?
You told me to go.

10:44.143 --> 10:47.063
Anyway, going to Gapyeong
for duck soup isn't a good idea.

11:14.382 --> 11:17.676
The briefing of July 29th will begin.

11:17.760 --> 11:20.846
Currently, the lower atmosphere is filled
with hot and humid air,

11:20.930 --> 11:24.350
and the upper layer is filled
with dry and hot air in Korea.

11:24.892 --> 11:26.477
The cause of the heatwave is

11:26.560 --> 11:29.522
the expansion of the North Pacific's
anticyclone in the south of Korea

11:29.605 --> 11:30.731
and the influence

11:30.815 --> 11:33.234
of the Tibetan anticyclone
in the inland of China.

11:42.701 --> 11:45.746
ELECTRONIC CIVIL SERVICE CENTER
DIVORCE

11:52.086 --> 11:53.671
PETITION FOR DIVORCE

12:23.617 --> 12:25.161
What was that for?

12:27.163 --> 12:28.539
I thought you weren't coming.

12:29.123 --> 12:31.000
I told you I had one more field trip.

12:31.083 --> 12:32.334
When is it over?

12:32.418 --> 12:35.045
I have a weather chart drawing class left.

12:35.129 --> 12:37.339
Do you want to have lunch
with me after that?

12:37.423 --> 12:38.883
At the KMA cafeteria?

12:38.966 --> 12:39.925
It's really good.

12:40.009 --> 12:41.218
Well…

12:41.969 --> 12:43.012
okay.

12:45.806 --> 12:47.016
What time?

12:47.099 --> 12:49.101
Call me when you're done.

12:49.185 --> 12:50.561
I'll come, okay?

12:50.644 --> 12:51.729
Okay.

12:53.397 --> 12:55.065
Pardon? Tomorrow?

12:55.149 --> 12:56.192
Yes.

12:57.651 --> 12:59.612
- Is it too soon?
- Of course, it is.

12:59.695 --> 13:01.280
I thought he'd go next week.

13:01.363 --> 13:04.617
You know how impatient Director Sung
of the typhoon center is.

13:05.367 --> 13:09.121
She's been pestering me since last week
about dispatching an officer.

13:09.622 --> 13:12.958
She said that he should be familiar
with related tasks in advance

13:13.042 --> 13:16.504
so that there will be no mistakes
even if a typhoon comes suddenly.

13:16.587 --> 13:17.838
What can I say to that?

13:17.922 --> 13:20.633
Still, you know how busy Headquarters is

13:20.716 --> 13:23.093
because of the heatwave.

13:23.594 --> 13:26.847
You can cover
the severe weather conditions there,

13:26.931 --> 13:28.057
can't you?

13:28.807 --> 13:30.434
- Well…
- That's not right.

13:30.518 --> 13:32.937
I told him yesterday that he'd be going.

13:33.521 --> 13:35.481
- He needs time to get ready.
- It's okay.

13:37.441 --> 13:38.734
It's okay, right?

13:38.817 --> 13:41.946
Yes. I can cover
the severe weather conditions there,

13:42.029 --> 13:43.364
so it won't be a problem.

13:43.948 --> 13:45.032
It's done then.

13:45.616 --> 13:47.701
You can leave on the weekend.

13:47.785 --> 13:48.953
Okay. We're done here.

13:50.996 --> 13:52.331
Jeez.

14:03.467 --> 14:05.219
Why did you say yes just like that?

14:05.302 --> 14:07.721
You aren't ready.
How will you go there tomorrow?

14:07.805 --> 14:10.182
You said you didn't want
duck soup in Gapyeong.

14:10.266 --> 14:13.811
I have no plans for the weekend,
so I'll go work at the typhoon center.

14:15.312 --> 14:17.106
Is this a joke or are you really upset?

14:17.189 --> 14:19.149
Half and half.

14:20.526 --> 14:22.653
Let's talk to the Director General again.

14:23.279 --> 14:24.738
Why do you

14:24.822 --> 14:26.907
keep confusing me?

14:30.202 --> 14:31.120
What do you mean?

14:31.203 --> 14:34.373
I thought you wanted
some time alone away from me.

14:35.666 --> 14:38.294
Isn't that why you asked me
to go to Jeju Island?

14:38.919 --> 14:42.047
Now that I'm leaving tomorrow,
why are you acting like this?

14:46.385 --> 14:48.220
I think you're mistaken.

14:48.304 --> 14:52.057
I never let my personal feelings
intervene in my work.

14:52.141 --> 14:54.643
It's never happened
in my previous relationships.

14:58.981 --> 15:01.817
You don't have to talk
to the Director General again.

15:01.901 --> 15:04.445
I'll go to Jeju Island tomorrow,

15:04.528 --> 15:05.905
Director Jin.

15:26.884 --> 15:28.218
- Reporter Cho.
- Yes?

15:28.719 --> 15:31.013
Didn't Reporter Chae come
to the KMA today?

15:31.680 --> 15:35.059
Well, I heard she took a leave.

15:35.142 --> 15:36.518
Didn't you know?

15:37.603 --> 15:39.730
Was that today?

15:40.356 --> 15:41.482
Yes.

15:42.066 --> 15:44.777
I'm so forgetful these days.

15:44.860 --> 15:46.820
- Okay. Bye.
- Take care.

16:03.420 --> 16:06.298
WEATHER

16:15.724 --> 16:17.977
KI-JUN

16:28.654 --> 16:29.488
You're on leave?

16:31.991 --> 16:34.493
Are you really going to do this?
Where are you?

16:35.202 --> 16:37.746
Come home. Let's talk face to face.

16:46.296 --> 16:49.758
FLIGHT RESERVATION

16:52.219 --> 16:54.430
FROM SEOUL TO JEJU ISLAND

16:54.513 --> 16:56.890
BOOK A FLIGHT

17:13.240 --> 17:14.450
Yu-jin.

17:47.775 --> 17:49.526
What's up with the atmosphere in here?

17:52.279 --> 17:54.239
I think Director Jin and Forecaster Lee

17:54.323 --> 17:57.451
are upset because of
the Jeju typhoon center.

17:57.534 --> 17:59.203
Do something about it,
Assistant Director Oh.

17:59.286 --> 18:01.371
- Me?
- What?

18:04.500 --> 18:06.710
Did you say something,
Assistant Director Oh?

18:06.794 --> 18:07.711
Did I?

18:09.755 --> 18:11.381
Well…

18:13.383 --> 18:14.718
Director Jin.

18:15.511 --> 18:17.721
Should we have a staff dinner?

18:21.725 --> 18:23.018
A staff dinner?

18:23.727 --> 18:25.270
Yes. Well…

18:25.354 --> 18:27.689
Forecaster Lee is going
to Jeju Island tomorrow.

18:27.773 --> 18:31.527
He'll be back soon
because it's a temporary dispatch,

18:31.610 --> 18:33.779
but it'd be nice to have dinner together

18:33.862 --> 18:35.572
to wish him good luck.

18:36.156 --> 18:37.241
What do you think?

18:37.324 --> 18:38.200
That's a great idea.

18:39.910 --> 18:41.662
Yes, sure. A staff dinner.

18:42.871 --> 18:44.331
Seok-ho, you're in, right?

18:45.040 --> 18:47.501
- I have plans.
- Oh, I see.

18:47.584 --> 18:49.545
Can you move it to some other day?

18:49.628 --> 18:51.839
It's Chief Team Two's first staff dinner.

18:52.422 --> 18:54.675
That's right. It's our first staff dinner.

18:54.758 --> 18:57.052
Our team never had one before.

18:57.136 --> 19:00.681
Why don't you reschedule it
and join us, Assistant Director Shin?

19:00.764 --> 19:02.182
No, it's too important.

19:02.850 --> 19:04.059
I'm sorry.

19:04.143 --> 19:07.813
Well, if you can't make it, it's okay.

19:07.896 --> 19:08.981
All right.

19:09.982 --> 19:11.233
Pardon?

19:11.817 --> 19:14.278
Let's have a staff dinner
with whoever can make it.

19:14.945 --> 19:16.363
Is that okay, Forecaster Lee?

19:18.657 --> 19:19.658
Yes.

19:21.910 --> 19:24.496
Then I'll make a reservation.

19:54.651 --> 19:55.694
What's wrong?

19:55.777 --> 19:57.988
We're having a staff dinner for you.

20:02.951 --> 20:04.953
Why are you upset again?

20:06.496 --> 20:07.706
"Again"?

20:08.665 --> 20:11.418
When was I ever upset?
Why did you say "again"?

20:13.045 --> 20:15.589
Since you told me to go to Jeju Island,

20:15.672 --> 20:17.799
I've never acted like I was upset.

20:18.550 --> 20:21.136
- What's wrong with you, kid?
- I'm not a kid.

20:21.220 --> 20:22.554
I'm an adult.

20:22.638 --> 20:24.097
I'm your man.

20:40.030 --> 20:41.156
Hello.

20:41.240 --> 20:43.533
- Hi. Enjoy your lunch.
- Thanks.

20:43.617 --> 20:45.035
- Hello.
- Hello.

20:45.118 --> 20:47.037
- Who is she?
- She's my daughter.

20:47.120 --> 20:49.248
- Your daughter?
- You can go first.

20:49.331 --> 20:50.290
- Go ahead.
- Thank you.

20:52.417 --> 20:54.461
She's on a field trip.

20:54.544 --> 20:56.213
I see. She's so pretty.

20:56.296 --> 20:58.006
- Isn't she?
- Yes.

20:59.633 --> 21:00.676
Oh, right.

21:00.759 --> 21:04.554
Forecasters are the busiest people
at the KMA.

21:04.638 --> 21:07.432
Everyone here knows that,
so they let me eat first

21:07.516 --> 21:10.394
- to help me get back to work quickly.
- I see.

21:11.561 --> 21:12.646
Thank you.

21:17.484 --> 21:19.027
Have some vegetables.

21:22.990 --> 21:24.992
There are sausages too.

21:25.075 --> 21:27.828
I've had them since I was little.

21:28.537 --> 21:29.830
They're really good.

21:36.878 --> 21:38.630
Can we sit with you guys?

21:38.714 --> 21:40.549
- Yes.
- Of course.

21:40.632 --> 21:42.884
- I'll move over here.
- Okay. Thanks.

21:43.510 --> 21:45.345
This is my daughter Um Bo-mi.

21:45.429 --> 21:46.805
- Hi, Bo-mi.
- Hi.

21:46.888 --> 21:49.141
- Hello.
- Nice to meet you.

21:49.224 --> 21:52.144
They're my colleagues.
We're on the same team.

21:52.978 --> 21:54.146
Hello.

21:54.229 --> 21:55.397
- Hi.
- Hi.

21:55.480 --> 21:57.524
- She's pretty.
- Isn't she?

21:57.607 --> 21:59.151
I guess she takes after her mom.

21:59.234 --> 22:00.527
What do you mean?

22:00.610 --> 22:03.697
What? I can see
that she resembles her dad too.

22:03.780 --> 22:06.241
What brings you here to the KMA?

22:06.325 --> 22:08.493
- Are you here to see your dad?
- She's on a field trip.

22:08.577 --> 22:10.120
- Oh, field trip.
- I see.

22:10.203 --> 22:12.914
- Do you like science?
- Yes.

22:14.166 --> 22:15.667
How did you know?

22:15.751 --> 22:17.461
These days, kids accumulate points

22:17.544 --> 22:21.214
through going on field trips
that suit their aptitude.

22:21.298 --> 22:22.341
- I see.
- I see.

22:22.424 --> 22:24.384
You have his scientific brain too.

22:24.468 --> 22:26.470
You're the spitting image of your dad.

22:26.553 --> 22:28.597
- Am I?
- Don't you know?

22:28.680 --> 22:30.891
Your dad is
the best meteorologist in Korea.

22:30.974 --> 22:32.684
I'm not the best.

22:33.727 --> 22:34.561
You are.

22:36.897 --> 22:38.774
Try this, Bo-mi.

22:39.399 --> 22:42.110
Senior Forecaster Um.

22:42.194 --> 22:43.695
I didn't know you were so sweet

22:43.779 --> 22:46.073
because you're so scary
in the situation room.

22:46.573 --> 22:48.116
I'm jealous, Bo-mi.

22:50.827 --> 22:51.953
Senior Forecaster Um.

22:52.037 --> 22:53.997
Can I have a piece of ham please?

22:54.081 --> 22:55.332
- What was that?
- What?

22:55.415 --> 22:56.708
Can I?

22:57.375 --> 22:59.336
Eat what you have on your plate.

22:59.419 --> 23:00.337
Okay.

23:01.046 --> 23:02.297
Try it, Bo-mi.

23:03.882 --> 23:05.008
Try it.

23:15.393 --> 23:16.728
- Isn't it good?
- Isn't it good?

23:25.278 --> 23:26.571
Excuse me for a minute.

23:26.655 --> 23:27.781
- Yes.
- Okay.

23:29.908 --> 23:31.159
- Hello, Mother.
- Hi.

23:31.243 --> 23:33.453
You need to take
the kids home early today.

23:33.537 --> 23:35.956
- Pardon?
- Maybe it's the hot weather.

23:36.039 --> 23:38.708
My eyes hurt. I'm not feeling well.

23:39.626 --> 23:42.003
I'm sorry, Mother.

23:42.087 --> 23:44.714
Chief Team Two is having
a staff dinner tonight.

23:45.590 --> 23:48.260
A severe weather forecaster
is going to Jeju Island.

23:48.343 --> 23:51.429
Our director arranged
this first staff dinner,

23:51.513 --> 23:52.681
so I can't miss it.

23:52.764 --> 23:56.101
Could you ask Jung-ho
to look after the kids just for today?

23:56.184 --> 23:58.103
He's studying though.

24:01.648 --> 24:05.819
I'll go home as soon as I can
after having dinner.

24:06.653 --> 24:08.446
Okay.

24:12.284 --> 24:13.994
Goodness, what should I do?

24:14.536 --> 24:17.539
I suggested the staff dinner,
so I can't miss it.

24:27.048 --> 24:28.466
I'm not a kid.

24:28.550 --> 24:29.801
I'm an adult.

24:30.343 --> 24:31.887
I'm your man.

24:33.680 --> 24:35.724
Hey, we're at the KMA.

24:35.807 --> 24:37.726
Then you should call me Forecaster Lee.

24:39.352 --> 24:42.314
I know you want to draw clear lines

24:43.148 --> 24:45.233
between the KMA, me, work, and dating.

24:45.317 --> 24:47.319
I understand that,

24:47.402 --> 24:49.988
and I want to cooperate
because I said I would.

24:50.071 --> 24:51.156
But…

24:53.408 --> 24:54.784
I'm me.

24:56.286 --> 24:58.538
I'm not your ex-boyfriend Han Ki-jun.

24:59.247 --> 25:00.373
It's me.

25:03.335 --> 25:06.004
So don't drag him into our relationship.

25:06.087 --> 25:09.382
I know what it was like with him,
how he hurt you,

25:09.466 --> 25:11.551
why you're so cautious
about dating at work,

25:11.635 --> 25:14.763
and why you're so worried
about getting caught.

25:15.388 --> 25:17.140
But that was your past relationship.

25:17.224 --> 25:19.100
Now you're with me.

25:20.894 --> 25:23.271
You compare me to him every time,

25:24.022 --> 25:25.482
and it really bothers me.

25:25.565 --> 25:27.984
When have I compared you to him?

25:30.070 --> 25:31.696
You keep me a secret.

25:32.364 --> 25:34.532
Also, you keep me at a distance,

25:34.616 --> 25:38.161
call me "kid,"
and don't take me seriously.

25:38.745 --> 25:40.622
It's because you're worried that

25:40.705 --> 25:42.415
I'd hurt you like Ki-jun did.

25:42.999 --> 25:44.209
You're worried about

25:45.210 --> 25:46.836
being embarrassed again.

25:47.629 --> 25:49.422
- Hey, Si-woo.
- That's right.

25:49.506 --> 25:51.132
I can't imagine being married.

25:51.216 --> 25:52.926
I just can't get married.

25:53.843 --> 25:57.097
Still, I want to love you.

25:59.599 --> 26:01.142
Because…

26:03.311 --> 26:05.063
I like you so much.

26:07.107 --> 26:08.149
But…

26:10.026 --> 26:12.195
if I confused you, then I'm sorry.

26:14.239 --> 26:16.116
I'm sorry I jumped at you to love you

26:17.242 --> 26:20.203
when I can't promise you anything.

26:20.287 --> 26:21.204
But…

26:23.331 --> 26:24.541
So…

26:25.834 --> 26:28.378
if you want to rethink our relationship,

26:31.214 --> 26:32.132
you can.

26:33.967 --> 26:37.178
But you need to be fully committed.

26:39.389 --> 26:43.393
Having a lukewarm relationship
where we keep a moderate distance…

26:43.977 --> 26:45.478
I can't do that.

26:47.105 --> 26:48.898
What do you mean by that?

26:53.778 --> 26:54.988
So…

26:56.448 --> 26:58.700
while I'm away on Jeju Island,
think about it.

26:59.743 --> 27:01.703
Whether you'll continue this relationship…

27:04.456 --> 27:05.707
or not.

27:34.694 --> 27:36.946
FATHER

28:02.347 --> 28:03.890
Yes, this is Jin Ha-kyung.

28:07.102 --> 28:09.729
I'll check and get back to you.

28:09.813 --> 28:10.647
Yes.

28:13.274 --> 28:16.069
KMA HEATWAVE FORECAST

28:19.155 --> 28:21.408
THE WORST HEATWAVE EVER!
THERE'S NO END TO IT

28:21.491 --> 28:23.660
PEOPLE ARE GROWING TIRED
OF THE MURDEROUS HEAT

28:28.498 --> 28:29.958
This is driving me nuts.

28:31.334 --> 28:33.545
I'm happy Bo-mi is here.

28:33.628 --> 28:34.587
Thank you.

28:37.465 --> 28:39.426
Where's Bo-mi?

28:39.509 --> 28:40.635
She's in the bathroom.

28:40.718 --> 28:42.303
- Have something to drink.
- Can I?

28:42.387 --> 28:43.930
- Yes.
- I want to try this.

28:45.140 --> 28:46.933
- Is it good?
- Yes.

29:29.267 --> 29:31.478
PETITION FOR DIVORCE

30:12.519 --> 30:14.687
Are you okay?

30:15.271 --> 30:18.650
Please call my dad.

30:19.609 --> 30:20.652
Goodness.

30:20.735 --> 30:22.153
- I'm so glad.
- You should be.

30:22.237 --> 30:23.613
I'm pretty fair-skinned.

30:23.696 --> 30:25.198
- What?
- She isn't just fair-skinned.

30:25.281 --> 30:26.574
Did you have lunch?

30:26.658 --> 30:27.867
- Yes.
- Hi, Forecaster Lee.

30:27.951 --> 30:31.204
- We ate already.
- Help! A student is down on the floor!

30:31.746 --> 30:33.456
A student collapsed in the bathroom,

30:33.540 --> 30:35.458
and she can't breathe!

30:37.043 --> 30:38.419
- Bo-mi.
- Oh, no!

30:38.503 --> 30:40.129
- Please call 911!
- Okay.

30:45.385 --> 30:48.429
EMERGENCY CENTER

30:49.055 --> 30:50.807
What happened to Bo-mi?

30:50.890 --> 30:52.809
I don't know.

30:53.393 --> 30:55.854
She was fine when we were having lunch,

30:55.937 --> 30:57.480
but she collapsed in the bathroom.

30:57.564 --> 31:00.859
She couldn't breathe
and had rashes on her face and neck.

31:00.942 --> 31:02.277
What did she eat?

31:02.360 --> 31:03.820
We ate in the cafeteria.

31:03.903 --> 31:05.405
What were the side dishes?

31:07.115 --> 31:09.117
Multi-grain rice.

31:09.200 --> 31:11.744
Seaweed soup, ham, and shredded radish.

31:12.787 --> 31:14.122
Did you give her ham?

31:14.706 --> 31:15.540
Yes.

31:15.623 --> 31:17.458
She's allergic to processed meat.

31:18.167 --> 31:19.919
Did you forget that?

31:21.546 --> 31:23.423
Try this, Bo-mi.

31:32.307 --> 31:33.641
- Isn't it good?
- Isn't it good?

31:36.978 --> 31:37.854
Goodness.

31:56.706 --> 31:58.666
"The worst heatwave ever!
There's no end to it."

31:58.750 --> 32:00.668
"People are growing tired
of the murderous heat."

32:01.336 --> 32:03.963
I asked you to stop these articles
from being published.

32:07.008 --> 32:08.426
Deputy Director Han!

32:09.010 --> 32:10.511
Yu-jin left.

32:11.095 --> 32:11.971
What?

32:12.055 --> 32:13.765
She wants a separation.

32:15.808 --> 32:16.726
Why?

32:19.896 --> 32:21.898
What am I going to do, Ha-kyung?

32:44.087 --> 32:45.129
Yes, Mom.

32:46.172 --> 32:48.675
How are you? Is everything okay?

32:51.552 --> 32:54.138
I called to hear your voice. I miss you.

32:57.558 --> 32:59.102
Ki-jun is doing well too.

33:01.270 --> 33:03.731
She won't answer my calls.

33:04.232 --> 33:06.109
She doesn't even check my texts.

33:06.192 --> 33:08.277
Why did this happen?

33:09.070 --> 33:11.906
Was it because she had lived with Si-woo?

33:15.994 --> 33:17.954
Or did something else happen?

33:18.037 --> 33:19.163
Hey.

33:20.039 --> 33:21.582
You know what?

33:21.666 --> 33:23.710
When we were together,

33:23.793 --> 33:27.088
you made me feel like
I was less important than your work.

33:28.923 --> 33:32.093
And whenever I felt like I was really
less valuable than your work,

33:32.176 --> 33:33.886
I was upset.

33:33.970 --> 33:35.972
I also felt like an immature loser

33:36.055 --> 33:39.642
for getting upset over such a thing.

33:42.854 --> 33:43.896
Was I like that?

33:44.647 --> 33:45.690
Yes.

33:46.190 --> 33:47.525
You're like that.

33:48.484 --> 33:50.403
When you say
let's not mix business with pleasure,

33:50.486 --> 33:51.863
you sound authoritative.

33:53.781 --> 33:56.409
Of course I knew that you were
speaking to a spokesperson,

33:56.492 --> 33:58.327
but I was your boyfriend first.

33:59.537 --> 34:01.873
The way you spoke to me often upset me.

34:03.791 --> 34:05.126
I know you want to

34:05.209 --> 34:07.045
draw clear lines

34:07.128 --> 34:09.172
between the KMA, me, work, and dating.

34:09.255 --> 34:11.257
I understand that,

34:11.340 --> 34:13.926
and I want to cooperate
because I said I would.

34:14.010 --> 34:14.886
But…

34:15.887 --> 34:17.180
But…

34:20.183 --> 34:21.809
One day I realized that

34:21.893 --> 34:24.270
I was doing the same thing to Yu-jin.

34:25.146 --> 34:28.357
I compared her to you every time.

34:29.233 --> 34:31.027
But that was your past relationship.

34:31.110 --> 34:32.779
Now you're with me.

34:33.362 --> 34:35.448
You compare me to him every time,

34:36.949 --> 34:38.284
and it really bothers me.

34:41.245 --> 34:44.207
Yu-jin is Yu-jin.

34:45.541 --> 34:47.001
I'm me.

34:47.085 --> 34:49.128
I'm not the Han Ki-jun
you dated in the past.

34:49.212 --> 34:50.713
I'm me.

34:50.797 --> 34:53.382
So don't get him involved
in your relationship with me.

35:07.688 --> 35:10.775
Yes. Don't worry. I got everything.

35:11.567 --> 35:12.985
You're here.

35:13.069 --> 35:14.862
Senior Forecaster Um's daughter is okay.

35:14.946 --> 35:17.865
It looks like the worst is over.

35:18.574 --> 35:19.784
I'm glad to hear that.

35:20.535 --> 35:22.036
The staff dinner tonight--

35:22.120 --> 35:24.872
Forecaster Lee will come
straight to the restaurant.

35:24.956 --> 35:26.874
Mr. Um will check his daughter's condition

35:26.958 --> 35:28.292
and join us later.

35:29.836 --> 35:30.795
Okay.

35:47.311 --> 35:48.729
Drink this.

35:49.522 --> 35:50.606
Thanks.

35:58.030 --> 36:00.491
Studying was the easiest thing
in the world.

36:02.660 --> 36:05.872
Because you get good grades
when you know how to do it.

36:07.790 --> 36:10.835
But the weather and family,

36:10.918 --> 36:13.212
I have no idea what to do with them.

36:14.630 --> 36:16.340
There are no formulas

36:16.424 --> 36:17.717
or manuals.

36:18.968 --> 36:21.512
I don't know how to be a good dad.

36:22.930 --> 36:24.974
What do I have to do

36:26.058 --> 36:28.060
to become a good head of my household?

36:31.898 --> 36:34.025
Having such worries means that

36:34.775 --> 36:36.194
you're already a good father.

36:38.946 --> 36:40.323
You know,

36:40.990 --> 36:42.408
I've never seen my father

36:42.491 --> 36:45.411
worry about such a thing.

36:49.916 --> 36:51.918
I'm just saying.

37:03.763 --> 37:04.972
How's Bo-mi?

37:06.224 --> 37:07.183
She's okay now.

37:07.808 --> 37:11.229
She needs to finish the IV treatment,

37:11.312 --> 37:13.522
so she'll be discharged late at night.

37:14.315 --> 37:15.816
You should go.

37:18.236 --> 37:20.196
I thought her atopy was cured.

37:24.659 --> 37:27.161
Do you think this kind of condition
can heal on its own?

37:28.246 --> 37:30.456
I check what she eats and wears.

37:30.539 --> 37:32.708
I even look after her while she sleeps.

37:32.792 --> 37:34.543
That's why she's healthy.

37:37.129 --> 37:38.089
I'm sorry.

37:38.714 --> 37:39.590
For what?

37:39.674 --> 37:41.509
I know nothing about Bo-mi,

37:41.592 --> 37:44.345
but I pretended to be a good dad
and made her sick.

37:45.680 --> 37:46.889
Exactly.

37:49.225 --> 37:51.894
So don't even try
when you know nothing about her.

38:15.793 --> 38:17.712
- Are you going out?
- What?

38:17.795 --> 38:20.506
Yes. I have an interview.

38:21.090 --> 38:22.300
Where are you going, Mom?

38:22.383 --> 38:24.385
Where are you going at night?

38:25.094 --> 38:26.971
Are you going to Ha-kyung's again?

38:27.054 --> 38:30.224
Do you think I have nowhere else to go?

38:30.308 --> 38:31.684
Don't you?

38:32.852 --> 38:33.811
Don't be home late.

38:34.478 --> 38:36.063
And don't drink too much.

38:43.279 --> 38:45.656
MOTHER-IN-LAW

38:54.290 --> 38:57.209
- Will you be okay?
- What?

38:57.293 --> 39:00.379
Isn't that your mother-in-law?
She keeps calling you.

39:01.422 --> 39:03.174
I'm sure she'll call her son

39:03.257 --> 39:05.217
if she needs help.

39:05.843 --> 39:07.511
But he's studying.

39:08.095 --> 39:11.432
And I'm the breadwinner
who works hard for the family.

39:11.515 --> 39:14.560
I need a break like this
to catch my breath.

39:15.186 --> 39:16.937
I'm going to eat,

39:17.021 --> 39:19.690
drink, and get drunk tonight.
Let's go to a karaoke too.

39:22.318 --> 39:25.196
By the way, where do you think
Assistant Director Shin went?

39:25.279 --> 39:27.323
He usually goes straight home after work.

39:27.907 --> 39:29.658
Does he have a girlfriend?

39:29.742 --> 39:32.328
It wouldn't be strange if he had one.

39:34.955 --> 39:37.416
- Director Jin. Over here.
- Over here.

39:46.801 --> 39:48.344
I can see

39:48.969 --> 39:51.097
you worked hard to draw these.

39:52.390 --> 39:53.766
So what?

39:53.849 --> 39:56.894
I have no idea where to start.

39:59.313 --> 40:01.107
Why did you choose a penguin?

40:02.525 --> 40:03.484
Because it's cute.

40:03.567 --> 40:05.403
Can you be more specific?

40:06.862 --> 40:09.448
First of all, it looks adorable,

40:09.532 --> 40:11.534
and the way it walks is cute.

40:12.535 --> 40:16.622
Waddle, waddle.

40:18.791 --> 40:19.834
But…

40:19.917 --> 40:23.754
it doesn't walk like that
because it wants to look cute.

40:24.630 --> 40:25.464
Pardon?

40:26.382 --> 40:29.802
The reason penguins waddle

40:29.885 --> 40:33.764
is because of the pendulum principle.

40:33.848 --> 40:37.685
When the clock pendulum
reaches one vertex,

40:37.768 --> 40:42.231
it stops for a moment to convert
potential energy into kinetic energy.

40:45.651 --> 40:46.569
Yes.

40:48.571 --> 40:50.948
I didn't know that. And?

40:52.199 --> 40:53.033
Pardon?

40:53.701 --> 40:54.785
And?

40:55.661 --> 40:56.787
Well…

40:58.122 --> 41:01.375
- If it waddles like that,
- Yes.

41:01.459 --> 41:04.753
it can store 80 percent
of its energy in its body.

41:04.837 --> 41:06.130
It can store energy.

41:07.798 --> 41:10.092
What's surprising is that

41:10.176 --> 41:13.345
the principle is very scientific.

41:13.429 --> 41:14.930
Is that so?

41:15.014 --> 41:16.056
Yes.

41:19.226 --> 41:20.311
Scientific principle…

41:23.439 --> 41:24.773
Also…

41:25.524 --> 41:28.694
their blood vessels
are woven closely together.

41:28.777 --> 41:33.032
It's called "wonderful net."
The arteries and veins are intertwined.

41:33.115 --> 41:36.410
Gosh, you know so much.

41:36.494 --> 41:39.038
I told you that you were a scientist.

41:39.121 --> 41:40.331
No, I'm not.

41:46.879 --> 41:48.380
I guess everyone's running late.

41:48.464 --> 41:51.008
Yes, they said they'd be late.

41:51.717 --> 41:56.639
Why don't we order something? I'm hungry.

41:56.722 --> 41:58.432
Yes, please go ahead.

41:58.516 --> 41:59.600
Okay.

42:00.226 --> 42:02.603
- What do you want?
- I think everyone eats pork belly here.

42:03.604 --> 42:05.564
- Shall we get pork belly?
- Yes.

42:19.495 --> 42:20.329
Hey.

42:27.878 --> 42:31.090
Eat up. Young people like this, right?

42:31.173 --> 42:32.508
Yes.

42:32.591 --> 42:35.010
But why did you want to see me?

42:35.094 --> 42:38.138
Let's eat first, then talk. Here.

42:48.482 --> 42:49.483
Well…

42:50.484 --> 42:52.695
how is Ha-kyung?

42:54.113 --> 42:58.117
She's probably very busy
because of the heatwave.

42:59.285 --> 43:02.663
Did she say anything after I came by?

43:02.746 --> 43:05.124
No. She didn't say anything.

43:07.459 --> 43:09.211
She caught me off guard that day.

43:10.713 --> 43:12.965
She suddenly said
she wouldn't get married,

43:13.048 --> 43:17.595
so I totally lost my pace and backed off.

43:18.470 --> 43:20.097
Well…

43:20.180 --> 43:22.099
the bachelor upstairs--

43:22.182 --> 43:24.560
Seok-ho is not for her.

43:24.643 --> 43:25.686
Why not?

43:25.769 --> 43:27.229
He doesn't get along with her.

43:27.313 --> 43:30.190
Personality, tastes, hobbies, lifestyle…

43:30.274 --> 43:32.109
None of them match.

43:32.776 --> 43:34.361
I know them well.

43:34.445 --> 43:37.990
You have to work things out
when you get married.

43:38.073 --> 43:40.951
Two people are raised by
different sets of parents.

43:41.035 --> 43:43.120
They lived in
two different worlds for years.

43:43.203 --> 43:46.248
How can they be hand-in-glove overnight?

43:46.332 --> 43:48.292
It'd be weird if they were.

43:50.836 --> 43:53.088
You're right about that.

43:53.172 --> 43:55.007
A married couple

43:55.090 --> 43:58.260
isn't a union of two complete people.

43:58.844 --> 44:00.220
Two people have to

44:00.304 --> 44:03.390
come together and become one.

44:04.183 --> 44:07.436
That process is called married life.

44:07.519 --> 44:09.730
That's how a married couple
becomes complete.

44:11.023 --> 44:12.816
Young people these days

44:12.900 --> 44:17.821
think of marriage
as some kind of practical insurance.

44:17.905 --> 44:19.907
That's why they can't even start.

44:20.407 --> 44:23.619
Because they look
at conditions and benefits first.

44:24.828 --> 44:27.581
Haven't you ever regretted it?

44:28.248 --> 44:29.375
Regretted what?

44:29.458 --> 44:31.502
Your marriage.

44:34.463 --> 44:35.798
Well…

44:35.881 --> 44:37.716
I regret it every day.

44:37.800 --> 44:41.387
I call him "that bastard."
And I say I hope he goes to hell.

44:42.012 --> 44:43.097
But…

44:43.639 --> 44:46.642
if you ask me if I'd go back in time

44:47.226 --> 44:51.355
and get married again, I think I would.

44:52.147 --> 44:53.357
Why?

44:55.192 --> 44:58.237
There were good times
because we were together.

44:58.320 --> 45:00.656
I had Tae-kyung and Ha-kyung.

45:00.739 --> 45:05.828
Those two are
the best works I've ever made.

45:09.123 --> 45:09.957
Hey.

45:10.666 --> 45:11.917
So--

45:12.000 --> 45:14.753
Still, it's not right.

45:14.837 --> 45:17.506
Seok-ho isn't for her.

45:18.048 --> 45:19.299
Never.

45:19.967 --> 45:21.844
Why are you so stern?

45:21.927 --> 45:23.095
Who are you to say no?

45:27.641 --> 45:29.685
The pizza is getting cold.

45:29.768 --> 45:32.604
Let's eat. I'll give you a slice.

46:05.137 --> 46:06.555
Today's staff dinner is a fail.

46:07.222 --> 46:08.223
What do you mean?

46:08.307 --> 46:11.226
We're eating delicious food.
It's going very well.

46:12.019 --> 46:13.228
Assistant Director Oh.

46:13.312 --> 46:15.689
Did you forget
why we're having this dinner?

46:15.772 --> 46:17.733
Number one. Forecaster Lee is leaving.

46:17.816 --> 46:20.694
Number two. This is the first staff dinner

46:20.777 --> 46:22.488
of Chief Team Two.

46:24.239 --> 46:25.407
What can we do?

46:25.908 --> 46:27.784
They don't want to come.

46:28.744 --> 46:30.996
Director Jin invited everyone,

46:31.079 --> 46:33.457
but they aren't showing up.

46:33.540 --> 46:35.042
There's nothing we can do.

46:36.627 --> 46:39.671
Since they aren't here,
let's order two more portions.

46:41.340 --> 46:43.008
We'll start the dinner again

46:43.091 --> 46:46.678
and call it Chief Team Two's
female pep rally.

46:46.762 --> 46:47.721
What do you say?

46:48.805 --> 46:50.057
Can we do that?

46:50.766 --> 46:51.808
All right.

46:51.892 --> 46:54.102
Ladies' dinner. I like that.

46:54.853 --> 46:57.272
Sir, give us
two more portions of pork belly

46:57.356 --> 46:59.483
- and soju please.
- Okay.

46:59.566 --> 47:00.651
Will you drink soju?

47:00.734 --> 47:03.237
Let's drink hard liquor
since we're starting over again.

47:03.862 --> 47:05.072
Are you okay with it?

47:06.073 --> 47:07.115
Thank you.

47:10.744 --> 47:13.080
Goodness.

47:16.708 --> 47:17.876
- Let's drink.
- Yes.

47:17.960 --> 47:19.086
All right.

47:22.422 --> 47:24.258
- How about karaoke?
- I love it.

47:24.341 --> 47:25.759
- Okay.
- Okay.

47:25.842 --> 47:26.802
- Cheers.
- Okay.

47:28.011 --> 47:30.055
- Let's go.
- Let's go.

47:30.138 --> 47:31.265
Round three!

47:33.350 --> 47:36.770
Wait. Let's go home.

47:36.853 --> 47:39.106
- What are you saying?
- Come on.

47:39.189 --> 47:42.234
- You're such a good singer.
- She is.

47:42.776 --> 47:44.403
I'm a high soprano.

47:44.486 --> 47:49.324
- High soprano.
- Songs in low-keys aren't even songs.

47:49.408 --> 47:51.577
I'm a baritone.

47:52.369 --> 47:53.495
I'm…

48:04.298 --> 48:07.301
DIRECTOR JIN HA-KYUNG

48:28.405 --> 48:29.740
Yes, Assistant Director Oh.

48:32.409 --> 48:33.827
Where are you?

48:37.998 --> 48:41.043
Director Jin is very drunk,

48:41.126 --> 48:43.795
but I have to go home.

48:43.879 --> 48:46.632
I'm sorry but can you come here right now?

48:53.847 --> 48:55.182
I'm here.

48:59.478 --> 49:00.854
Are you drunk?

49:03.106 --> 49:04.358
Can you walk?

49:15.369 --> 49:17.162
I want to make it work.

49:19.748 --> 49:22.292
I want things to work out between us.

49:28.548 --> 49:29.675
But…

49:31.760 --> 49:33.345
this is all I can do.

49:35.889 --> 49:38.350
Loving someone moderately,

49:39.434 --> 49:40.977
liking them moderately,

49:41.478 --> 49:43.689
and being moderately stable
is what I like to do.

49:45.440 --> 49:47.693
When I go over that line,

49:50.487 --> 49:51.905
I become anxious.

49:55.826 --> 49:57.285
I feel like

49:58.328 --> 50:00.497
I'm a different person.

50:06.211 --> 50:07.504
So…

50:09.423 --> 50:11.216
I can only do it moderately.

50:14.928 --> 50:16.930
Get up. Let's go home.

50:17.931 --> 50:19.933
So you decide.

50:21.476 --> 50:23.895
Go to Jeju Island and make a decision.

50:29.568 --> 50:33.655
Think carefully about whether
you can be with me in moderation or not

50:34.156 --> 50:36.616
and make a decision.

50:41.997 --> 50:45.667
A senior forecaster once said this.

50:45.751 --> 50:50.088
"If you can't possibly understand
the satellite image,

50:50.756 --> 50:52.591
try observing

50:53.091 --> 50:56.344
the flow of clouds from a distance."

51:19.785 --> 51:23.413
To be honest,
I didn't understand him back then.

51:23.914 --> 51:27.626
I had never seen a satellite image
that I didn't understand,

51:27.709 --> 51:31.505
and I was more confident
about the weather than anyone else.

51:36.176 --> 51:37.427
Then…

51:38.386 --> 51:39.888
I met you.

52:10.836 --> 52:12.212
Gosh, my head hurts.

52:21.263 --> 52:22.264
Hey.

52:41.032 --> 52:41.908
What?

52:42.409 --> 52:44.160
Are you going straight to the airport?

52:45.370 --> 52:46.538
That's mine.

52:46.621 --> 52:47.706
You scared me.

52:51.793 --> 52:53.879
Are you going back home?

52:53.962 --> 52:56.089
It's typhoon season,

52:56.172 --> 52:58.008
so I'll stay at the KMA.

52:59.217 --> 53:00.468
What about Forecaster Lee?

53:00.552 --> 53:02.262
He left already.

53:02.345 --> 53:03.471
Pardon?

53:03.555 --> 53:07.225
He left for Jeju Island today.
Didn't you know?

53:09.394 --> 53:12.898
Have some soup while it's hot.
You must be hungover.

53:38.924 --> 53:40.175
You know what?

53:40.759 --> 53:44.804
You were the most
unpredictable weather for me.

53:56.650 --> 53:57.817
I…

53:59.527 --> 54:00.612
There was an accident?

54:00.695 --> 54:02.072
How badly hurt is he?

54:02.155 --> 54:03.073
No…

54:03.865 --> 54:05.158
Who am I speaking to?

54:05.241 --> 54:06.743
Can you tell me what hospital--

54:06.826 --> 54:08.286
This is Chae Yu-jin.

54:15.460 --> 54:17.128
I'm with Si-woo right now.

54:45.573 --> 54:46.533
Hello?

54:47.659 --> 54:49.202
What's up at this hour?

54:51.579 --> 54:52.706
What?

54:56.584 --> 54:59.379
Ha-kyung. What's going on?

54:59.963 --> 55:01.423
Si-woo is hurt.

55:01.506 --> 55:03.216
Okay, so he's hurt.

55:03.299 --> 55:05.135
Why is Yu-jin there with him?

55:05.719 --> 55:07.470
- By chance.
- What?

55:08.596 --> 55:10.557
They ran into each other
on Jeju Island by chance.

55:14.728 --> 55:16.604
EMERGENCY MEDICAL CENTER

55:35.915 --> 55:37.167
Goodness.

55:44.299 --> 55:46.009
This is all because of you.

55:46.593 --> 55:47.927
Why is this because of me?

55:48.011 --> 55:50.096
Because our failed relationship

55:50.180 --> 55:51.806
left me wounded,

55:51.890 --> 55:54.142
I was really edgy and cranky toward him.

55:54.726 --> 55:59.272
Well, you were edgy and cranky
when you were with me too.

55:59.355 --> 56:01.274
Because of you,

56:02.609 --> 56:04.069
I got scared.

56:04.778 --> 56:06.821
I was scared of getting hurt again.

56:07.655 --> 56:09.532
So I couldn't show him how I felt.

56:11.493 --> 56:13.328
I wasn't able to do anything.

56:17.123 --> 56:18.583
What am I going to do?

56:19.626 --> 56:21.127
What am I going to do now?

56:23.046 --> 56:24.964
What am I going to do now?

56:35.058 --> 56:39.646
So it wasn't because
Si-woo never wanted to get married.

56:41.272 --> 56:43.024
I was afraid that it'd get too hot,

56:43.858 --> 56:45.819
that I wouldn't be able to handle it,

56:46.402 --> 56:48.822
that I wouldn't be able to
control my feelings,

56:49.364 --> 56:51.366
so I didn't raise the last 1°C

56:52.742 --> 56:54.285
to the boiling point

56:54.369 --> 56:57.080
by doing everything in moderation.

56:57.997 --> 56:59.165
But…

57:06.047 --> 57:08.216
- Senior Forecaster Um.
- Yes?

57:13.012 --> 57:15.598
When did it become like that?

57:26.484 --> 57:29.279
This is Um Dong-han of Headquarters.

57:30.321 --> 57:32.073
We just saw it.

57:32.157 --> 57:33.700
Is it what I think it is?

57:33.783 --> 57:34.701
Yes.

57:34.784 --> 57:37.704
It's Typhoon Number 15 Elisha
that followed Number 14 Ricky.

57:38.288 --> 57:41.624
Around 11 o'clock today,
it was moving northeast

57:41.708 --> 57:44.377
with a central pressure of 990mb,
a maximum wind speed of 20m per second,

57:44.461 --> 57:47.964
and a strong wind radius of 150
from 300km west of Okinawa.

57:48.047 --> 57:49.090
Hey.

57:49.174 --> 57:50.425
Bring it to me.

57:50.508 --> 57:52.135
NATIONAL TYPHOON CENTER

57:52.218 --> 57:53.553
Satellite Center?

57:53.636 --> 57:54.888
What's the intensity of the typhoon?

57:54.971 --> 57:59.559
At 10 p.m., it'll advance
from 120km west of Okinawa

57:59.642 --> 58:03.188
to the southern sea of Jeju
with a central air pressure of 980mb,

58:03.271 --> 58:06.691
a maximum wind speed of 28m per second,
and a strong wind radius of 200.

58:08.776 --> 58:11.237
Okay. Got it.

58:11.321 --> 58:13.740
Keep sending the data please.

58:14.866 --> 58:15.992
- Assistant Director Shin.
- Yes.

58:16.075 --> 58:18.203
Give me the hourly data
on the changes in the ocean heat content

58:18.286 --> 58:19.329
- Okay.
- Assistant Director Oh.

58:19.412 --> 58:21.915
Identify the vertical wind shear
and steering flow

58:21.998 --> 58:23.374
- from the new prediction data.
- Okay.

58:23.458 --> 58:24.959
VERTICAL WIND SHEAR:
CHANGE IN WINDSPEED WITH HEIGHT

58:25.043 --> 58:26.794
STEERING FLOW: THE FLOW
THAT INFLUENCES TYPHOON MOVEMENT

58:55.907 --> 58:59.452
I'm going to kill you all.

59:44.247 --> 59:49.377
INNOVATIVE WEATHER SERVICES
A STEPPING STONE TO PUBLIC SAFETY

01:00:27.165 --> 01:00:29.876
I didn't know you loved Si-woo this much.

01:00:29.959 --> 01:00:31.002
I don't know anything anymore.

01:00:31.085 --> 01:00:33.755
I don't know where it all went wrong.

01:00:33.838 --> 01:00:35.256
I want to speak to the person in charge.

01:00:35.340 --> 01:00:37.050
- How do you expect me to?
- What's going on?

01:00:37.133 --> 01:00:38.926
- You're obstructing official duties.
- Stay away.

01:00:39.010 --> 01:00:40.887
That's how important this room is.

01:00:41.679 --> 01:00:42.513
I can't do this anymore.

01:00:42.597 --> 01:00:45.933
Just be a man and sign the divorce papers.

01:00:46.517 --> 01:00:48.770
Yu-jin just happened
to leave me right now.

01:00:48.853 --> 01:00:49.979
Please let me go.

01:00:50.063 --> 01:00:52.982
I'll join you on that flight
to Jeju Island tomorrow.

01:00:53.066 --> 01:00:56.611
There are many things
we wouldn't know unless we express them.

01:00:56.694 --> 01:00:59.864
So why did we expect each other
to realize those things

01:00:59.947 --> 01:01:01.741
- without saying anything?
- Yu-jin.

01:01:01.824 --> 01:01:04.911
I just wanted to have
some personal time together.

01:01:04.994 --> 01:01:08.081
Where did we go wrong?

01:01:09.290 --> 01:01:14.295
Subtitle translation by: Soo-hyun Yang
